      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Or you could just add a number to each one. Then when youre finished and have the final one, just remember the number of that avatar, delete the others and reupload the last one to rename it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-12T20:37:31.037Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While making an avatar, people usually upload a few versions of their avatar and test them out in game before settling on a version they're satisfied with. To clear up their avatar selection menu, they would then delete previous versions of the avatar using the SDK's \"Manage Uploaded Content\" feature. However, this feature only displays the name of the avatar and a picture of the model with no way to tell which is the most current version. \n\nAs such, I think it'd be a great idea to include a timestamp on when the avatars were uploaded, thus preventing confusion and deleting the wrong avatar.",
